  "note": "First election of the Castleblayney No. 2 rural district council (the Co. Armagh part of Castleblayney union, also called Crossmaglen Rural District), polled 6 April 1899; two councillors for each division. The nomination list also prints \"Crossmaglen—James Hale and Patrick M'Shane, sen., P.L.G.\", a second entry for Crossmaglen that is probably another division misnamed; it is not filed. Polled 6 April 1899; \"the first two in each division were declared elected\". Printed \"Dorsey\" (Dorsy). P. Markey was also nominated."
